==Old Norse==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*stainaz||stone}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term/t|ang|stān}}, {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term/t|ofs|stēn}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term/t|osx|stēn}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term/t|goh|stein}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term/t|got|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌹𐌽𐍃|tr=[[stains#Gothic|stains]]|sc=Goth}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*stāi-||something hard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|12th century Icelandic}} {{IPA|lang=non|/stɛinː/}}

===Noun===
{{non-noun|m|steins|steinar}}
# [[stone]], [[boulder]], [[rock]]
#* ''Barlaams Saga'', p. 167
#** ...meistara a '''stein''' eða gullsmiða eða tresmiða eða annarra hagleiksmanna.
#*** ...master of '''stone''' or goldsmith or carpenter or any other crasftsman.
# [[precious stone]]
# [[calculus]], [[stone]] in the [[bladder]]
# [[paint]]
# [[stone]] [[building]], [[cloister]], [[cell]]

====Declension====
{{non-decl-m-a|stein|stein|ns=steinn}}

